wpe-tsp on Mortar: the changes to upstream's app/ (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Stanislav Matveyev).
It stays an SDL2 program and reaches the shell through sdl2-compat and sdl3-pvr (see default.nix).
- The pad is the shell's per-app virtual pad: map its evdev buttons to what the stock pad reports.
- Pause when the shell suspends the window: unmap the WPE view, skip swaps, slow the input tick.
- Keyboards and mice read from evdev are dropped while not on screen (nothing grabs them).
- Settings under ~/.config, downloads under ~/.local/share, no paths on /mnt or in /tmp.
- No mpv, yt-dlp or RustyPipe: their settings go, YouTube plays in the page.

